{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "the-boundary-check-catches-a-harness-reach-and-a-second-writ",
  "title": "The boundary check catches a harness reach and a second writer, and passes a lawful plugin",
  "requirement": "Outside the harness seam, kit code does not import the harness's internals, and every state has one writer: a change that breaks either boundary is refused by scripts/check-boundaries.mjs --check with exit 1, while a plugin that uses the declared plugin API and writes its own file passes with exit 0.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "verified",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "scripts/check-boundaries.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test scripts/check-boundaries.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "The test builds a temporary tree with plugins/pilot-breach/seam.mjs (imports @deepseek-ai/dsh-session and @deepseek-ai/dsh-tools/lib/index.js), plugins/pilot-breach/board.mjs (writeFileSync into .dsh/taskboard.rows.json) and plugins/pilot-legal/tool.mjs (imports @deepseek-ai/dsh-tools, writes its own .dsh/pilot-legal.json).",
    "scan() over the lawful tree: no findings. scan() over each breach: the two harness reaches and the second writer are named.",
    "main(['--check','--root',breachTree]) exits 1; main(['--check','--root',lawfulTree]) exits 1 as well because every named exception is stale in a tree that holds none of the excepted files; report mode exits 0.",
    "Observed as a product run first: node scripts/check-boundaries.mjs --check on a copy of the kit's plugins/scripts/profile with the two breach modules present exited 1 with three findings; with the breach removed and the lawful plugin left in place it exited 0 with five excepted findings."
  ],
  "expected": "The breach tree is refused with exit 1 and the findings name the rule, the file and the literal; a lawful plugin alone produces no finding; a tree whose exceptions match nothing is refused, so the exception list cannot rot.",
  "tags": [
    "boundaries",
    "architecture",
    "harness-seam",
    "one-writer"
  ],
